# Local-only. This repo is public; these stay on the laptop.
#   - the architecture PDF is the design source of truth and Blarmo holds the copy (his README says so)
#   - the desktop screenshot is a screenshot of somebody's desktop
#   - the vendor metadata dumps are 1.6 MB of HuggingFace API echo
# NOTE ON IMAGES: there used to be blanket `*.png` / `*.jpg` lines here, which meant git silently
# refused every image in the project - art candidates, UI captures, a reference frame from the die.
# Screenshots are private because of *which* screenshots they are, not because PNGs are dangerous, so
# the rule is now by path (`journal/`, `shots/`, `capture/`) and never by image extension. Adding an
# extension ban back is a bug; test/ignore_test.mjs fails if one appears.
*.pdf
notes/hf_api.json
notes/hf_tree.json
notes/type_enum.json

# No image extension is banned anywhere in this file - Blarmo's call, 2026-11-08, and
# test/ignore_test.mjs fails the tree if one comes back. Pre-made art under game/art/ ships with the
# game, and so does the art the table paints: a live Anima render of a room somebody described, or of
# Glim the merchant, is written to game/art/<style>/ and committed with the seed that made it in
# manifest.json. That is deliberate - "say it and see it" means the thing you said is still there next
# Saturday - and the same sentence in the same style repaints the same picture, so nothing is lost by
# keeping it out. What IS private is private by path: journal/, shots/, capture/ above.

saves/
journal/
shots/
capture/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# Model weights never go in the repo - this repo is public and the DM model runs only on the
# laptop. Nothing enforced that rule: a stray dl_model/quant_scan run with a relative output path
# could drop a .gguf in-tree and `git add -A` would publish it. Ignore by extension so git refuses
# first; if a binary ever genuinely belongs in the tree, `git add -f path` says so on purpose.
*.gguf
*.gguf-*
*.safetensors
*.safetensors.index.json
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.ggml
*.bin
models/

# Which art style THIS machine chose. Mutable per-machine state, not content.
game/art/settings.json
